  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member with iCloud sync on, I want my recent rehost uploads to follow me to my other Apple devices, so that the composer's image picker shows them everywhere.\n\n### Operator decision (2026-11-16)\n\n- **Option A:** the rehost upload history syncs through the existing **iCloud key-value store** when iCloud sync is on. It also syncs **when sync is switched on**: the local history is pushed at activation.\n- Only the **100 most recent** images are synced; the full history stays on the device.\n- Sync off: nothing changes, device-only as today.\n- This changes ADR 0013 rules 2 and 3 (\"upload histories do not leave the device\"). It needs an **ADR 0013 amendment** in the same PR, merged by the core orchestrator.\n\n### Scope\n\n- The store: one KVS key `{version, items:[{id, fullURL, mediumURL?, previewURL?, miniURL?, addedAt}]}`, capped at 100 newest, about 30 KiB. Check the appendix budget (< 200 KiB total).\n- **Merge by id** (union of both devices' adds, newest first, cap 100). Do not use last-writer-wins on the whole list: adds made on two devices must both survive. Deletions, if the picker allows them: tombstones, or document the limit.\n- **Activation:** when the member turns iCloud sync on, merge the local history into the cloud one.\n- The Apple-ID change, quarantine and initial-sync rules of ADR 0013 (Amendments 1 and 2) apply as for the other lists.\n- Tests: merge (two devices), cap, activation push, account change, and an older build ignoring the new key.\n\n### Not in scope\n\n- The update path from the current app: LOT-067 already imports `Documents/rehostImagesSwiftUI.json` at first launch. An end-to-end TestFlight check is not planned (operator, 2026-11-16).\n- The old `rehostImages.plist` import: see its own issue.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
